# Path attributes for the Godot Card Game Framework.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why this repository does NOT use Git LFS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Images and fonts are ~9.9 MB of the ~13 MB working tree, which is the usual
# cue to reach for Git LFS. Do not. This repository is a public fork of
# db0/godot-card-game-framework, and GitHub refuses LFS uploads from a public
# fork:
#
#     batch response: can not upload new objects to public fork
#
# LFS objects are always billed to and stored against the root repository, so
# a fork cannot push its own. Adding "filter=lfs" rules here would silently
# rewrite assets into pointer files and produce commits that can never be
# pushed, and every clone without git-lfs installed would get unusable text
# stubs where its art and fonts should be.
#
# It is also unnecessary: the whole history is only ~7 MB because these assets
# almost never change. Plain git storage is the right call at this size.
#
# If Git LFS is ever genuinely needed, the fork must first be detached into a
# standalone repository (GitHub Support), and upstream merges will then
# conflict on every asset. Weigh that before starting.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary assets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# "binary" is shorthand for "-text -diff": never apply line-ending conversion
# and never attempt a textual diff. Without this, a contributor cloning on
# Windows with core.autocrlf=true relies purely on git's NUL-byte heuristic to
# avoid corrupting these files on checkout.

*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.bmp   binary
*.webp  binary
*.tga   binary
*.psd   binary

*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

*.ogg   binary
*.wav   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.ogv   binary
*.webm  binary

*.zip   binary

# Godot binary resources.
*.res   binary
*.scn   binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Godot text sources
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Godot always writes these with LF. Pinning eol=lf keeps Windows checkouts
# from reintroducing CRLF and producing whole-file diffs that hide the real
# change. Every one of these files is already LF, so this normalizes nothing
# today, it only stops the next Windows contributor from flipping them.

*.gd     text eol=lf
*.tscn   text eol=lf
*.tres   text eol=lf
*.import text eol=lf
*.cfg    text eol=lf
*.godot  text eol=lf

# Intentionally left unspecified: *.svg, *.json, *.md, *.txt, *.yml, *.html,
# *.fnt. Those files are checked in with CRLF today; declaring them here
# would renormalize them and bury real changes in unrelated churn.
